              "source_excerpt": "Trinity and Settlement say the project will deliver about 120 permanently affordable apartments, including homes for formerly homeless households, with outdoor-use space, food-learning space, and flexible community rooms; YIMBY adds a 24-story all-affordable tower with 18 formerly homeless set-asides and ground-floor social services; NYCEEC's January 2026 deal memo sizes the project at 120,372 square feet, roughly $109.4 million total cost, and a $4.4 million predevelopment loan supporting an all-electric Passive House build expected to finish in 2030.",
