              "source_excerpt": "6sqft reports Toll Brothers paid $53 million for the roughly 12,000-square-foot lot and plans an approximately 85,000-square-foot condominium, while Commercial Observer's site-marketing coverage called 118-120 Tenth Avenue one of the last development sites on the High Line and quantified the zoning envelope at about 66,100 square feet residential or 78,300 square feet commercial before additional air rights. Together they explain why the parcel kept resurfacing through Brandon Miller / GDS office concepts before the current residential pivot.",
